{
  "an10.84:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 10.84 ",
  "an10.84:0.2": "9. Senior Mendicants ",
  "an10.84:0.3": "Declaration ",
  "an10.84:1.1": "There Venerable Mahāmoggallāna addressed the mendicants: ",
  "an10.84:1.2": "“Reverends, mendicants!” ",
  "an10.84:1.3": "“Reverend,” they replied. ",
  "an10.84:1.4": "Venerable Mahāmoggallāna said this: ",
  "an10.84:2.1": "“Take a mendicant who declares enlightenment: ",
  "an10.84:2.2": "‘I understand: “Rebirth is ended, the spiritual journey has been completed, what had to be done has been done, there is nothing further for this place.”’ ",
  "an10.84:2.3": "They’re pursued, pressed, and grilled by the Realized One, or by one of his disciples who is a meditator skilled in attainments, in the minds of others, and in encompassing another’s mind. ",
  "an10.84:2.4": "Grilled in this way they get stuck or lose their way. They fall to ruin and disaster. ",
  "an10.84:3.1": "The Realized One or one of his disciples encompasses their mind and investigates: ",
  "an10.84:3.2": "‘Why does this venerable declare enlightenment, saying: ",
  "an10.84:3.3": "“I understand: ‘Rebirth is ended, the spiritual journey has been completed, what had to be done has been done, there is nothing further for this place’”?’ ",
  "an10.84:4.1": "They understand: ",
  "an10.84:5.1": "‘This venerable gets irritable, ",
  "an10.84:5.2": "and often lives with a heart full of anger. ",
  "an10.84:5.3": "But being full of anger means decline in the teaching a